==Trivia==
*She is based on the ''[[wikipedia:Baku (mythology)|baku]]'', a Japanese mythical creature that devours dreams.
**The Japanese term ''baku'' can also refer to a [[wikipedia:Malayan tapir|Malayan tapir]].
**The Japanese names of Bakoo's first two stages are both puns involving ''baku''. [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|Bombergirl]] is <u>Baku</u>dan Musume (バクダン娘, "Bomb Girl"), while [[Wrath of the Dreamer (Deadly)|Wrath of the Dreamer]] is <u>Baku</u>sui Musume (バクスイ娘, "Deep Sleep Girl").
*Her Japanese name, Yumemi-chan (ユメミちゃん), literally means "Dreaming-chan" or "Dream-chan". The honorific ''-chan'' is a cute-sounding term of endearment typically used for or between girls or small children, as well as a nickname among close friends, family members, or lovers.
*Among the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], Bakoo appears to represent the sin of sloth. In addition to her design and description, this is reflected in how she doesn't spawn on a timer in her debut stage like the other six bosses, only taking initiative after the enemy base is attacked.
*Her attack animation may take inspiration from the [https://www.pikminwiki.com/Fiery_Blowhog Fiery Blowhog] from the ''[[wikipedia:Pikmin|Pikmin]]'' series.
*Bakoo, [[Dark Cyclone]], [[Dark Lazer (Enemy)|Dark Lazer]], [[Two Can]], [[Black Marmod]], [[Commander Hannya]] and [[Perry Duche]] are the only [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]] whose eyes are not red.
*She has the lowest health and money drop of all [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] and is tied with [[Doremi]] for the shortest standing range and longest effective range of all Advent Bosses.
**She also has the longest effective range of all Dark enemies.

